WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:06.790
Legend tells of many ancient weapons, many
of them imbued with great power.

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:13.290
Hammers that can call forth the very forces
of the heavens themselves, raining down devastating

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:19.100
thunder storms and electrifying bolts of lightning
to vanquish any foe.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:24.870
Or, there’s the Arthurian myth of a blade
buried deep in the heart of a stone.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:30.609
To any ordinary person, the sword is unmovable,
it won’t budge no matter how much force

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:36.750
is exerted on it, or how physically strong
the person trying to pull it is.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:42.980
Only if one of purest heart, and truest virtue
should ever reach for its hilt, then the sword

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:47.890
will spring free, and grant the holder the
rightful rule over the land.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:54.940
But there is another weapon, another sword,
bestowed with a power as old as time itself.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:01:00.910
Some have heard tales that it was forged of
pure shadow, by a demon seeking dominion over

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:02.940
all creation.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:08.620
Other stories will claim the blade itself
is alive, and capable of bonding itself to

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:09.620
a host.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:15.010
While it grants its wielder the means to fell
an entire army with a swing of its blade,

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:21.830
the weapon also curses those who seek to covet
its destructive power, slowly destroying them

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:25.370
the longer they possess this unholy sword.

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:31.360
Such a powerful tool of devastation would
wreak chaos on this world and any other.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.850
But this…
well, this is not that sword at all.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:40.710
Actually, the ‘weapon’ in question – even
though it technically doesn’t count as one-

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:42.450
isn’t some magical item.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:47.220
In fact, its only real power is causing all
its various owners over the years to end up

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.290
needing a serious trip to the ER.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.680
So, this is SCP-572.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:58.430
Okay, sorry, I’ll do the voice again – but
this is the last time.

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:04.729
Or, as the legends call it, The Katana of
Apparent Invincibility!

00:02:04.729 --> 00:02:09.140
Now just like the ancient weapons of legend,
this katana has changed hands a number of

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:11.830
times over the course of human history.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:17.050
One of those to wield its completely un-incredible
power was Jonathan, a young man with high

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:20.030
hopes of going viral online as a master swordsman.

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:24.750
However, while most would only ever gain that
title after years’ worth of study, practicing

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:30.590
complex hand-to-hand combat forms, and learning
to respect the blade itself and the craftsmanship

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:32.080
used in making one…

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:38.670
Jonathan just read a WikiHow tutorial on sword
tricks and, deciding they looked easy enough,

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.400
decided that he could just wing it.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:45.610
Of course, the first step in becoming a master
swordsman – without putting in any of the

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:48.530
work – was to find an actual sword to use.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:54.030
And luckily, the pawn shop in Jonathan’s
hometown had the very answer to his low-effort

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.030
dreams.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:59.739
Hanging there behind the counter, displayed
on the top shelf with a thin layer of dust

00:02:59.739 --> 00:03:03.110
coating it, was the Katana of Apparent Invincibility.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:08.280
The store’s owner had long since forgotten
it was even there, and was happy enough to

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:11.200
mark the price down for the sake of getting
rid of it.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:16.560
The moment he held it in his hands, Jonathan
felt unstoppable, like he could conquer his

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.990
whole town with the power of this mighty sword,
that was barely sharp enough to cut wet toilet

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:22.990
paper.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:27.530
He knew it would only take one show of the
weapon’s very arguable might to cement him

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:29.959
as one of history’s greatest swordsmen.

00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:34.400
Unfortunately, the stunt that Jonathan attempted
went about as well as you’d expect.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.980
Naturally, an elaborate stunt involving a
blunt katana and Jonathan’s friend, Kali,

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:44.290
on a BMX bike was sure to be a perfectly safe
combination – any sane human being would

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.170
tell you that, right?

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:50.470
After setting up his phone at the skatepark
and hitting record, Jonathan called for Kali

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:55.370
to ride down one side of the half-pipe and
up the other, while he used his newfound sword

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:59.760
skills to cleave the front wheel of her bike
clean off in mid-air.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.780
Having been promised a replacement bike paid
for by all the hits this video would get online,

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:08.210
Kali went down, then up… then straight back
down.

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:13.190
Jonathan swung the blade, only for it to get
lodged in the wheel spokes, bringing his friend,

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:18.340
and the solid frame of her bike crashing down
on top him in a heap of tangled limbs and

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:19.340
metal.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:23.300
All the while, nearby skaters filmed the mess
on their phones; the ones who could hold back

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.210
their laughs anyway.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:31.199
Sometime after the skatepark debacle, SCP-572
would end up in the hands of yet another would-be

00:04:31.199 --> 00:04:35.210
swordsman, with just as… ‘impressive’
results.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:42.460
Martin Zeepleburger had grown into quite a
controversial figure over the years, garnering

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:47.699
his own legend of sorts, although not a reputation
that any mythical warrior of old would ever

00:04:47.699 --> 00:04:48.699
want.

00:04:48.699 --> 00:04:53.349
You see, Martin had founded a website that
had, in its earlier days, introduced the internet

00:04:53.349 --> 00:04:58.630
to a brand-new way of communicating and keeping
in touch with their friends and family.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:03.249
And, as a result, he had accumulated a staggering
amount of cash to show for it.

00:05:03.249 --> 00:05:07.089
But running a social media app didn’t keep
the lights on forever.

00:05:07.089 --> 00:05:12.330
Despite his company growing into a multi-million-dollar
corporation, the market had become saturated.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:17.161
More new and innovative sites run by Martin’s
competitors began appearing, each new one

00:05:17.161 --> 00:05:21.119
more unique than his had ever been back in
the early days.

00:05:21.119 --> 00:05:25.020
Keeping up and still making money was hard,
so Martin resorted to gathering the personal

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:30.150
data of the millions of users his site had
amassed over the years, and selling that information

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:33.020
to… well, anyone who would pay him.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:36.939
Understandably, people were a little upset
to hear that all their private information

00:05:36.939 --> 00:05:38.699
was being shared around so brazenly.

00:05:38.699 --> 00:05:44.339
That’s when rumors of Martin’s… interesting
behavior started to be made public by some

00:05:44.339 --> 00:05:46.379
of his former employees.

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:49.719
The internet had already been rife with jokes
at Martin’s expense.

00:05:49.719 --> 00:05:54.069
His stunted manner of speaking, strange barbequing
livestreams filmed in front of what looked

00:05:54.069 --> 00:05:59.129
like a green screen, along with many other
quirks were often the subject of ridicule.

00:05:59.129 --> 00:06:04.430
Some even speculated that he was a collection
of various things –a robot, an alien, even

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.930
an iguana – pretending to be a human being.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:13.349
Then there was his choice of office equipment;
specifically, a certain Katana of Apparent

00:06:13.349 --> 00:06:14.349
Invincibility.

00:06:14.349 --> 00:06:19.039
Given his considerable net worth, the programmers
working in the head offices of Martin’s

00:06:19.039 --> 00:06:23.219
social media company knew he had somewhat
expensive tastes.

00:06:23.219 --> 00:06:27.349
That was what made it all the more baffling
that he bought what looked to be a very poor-quality

00:06:27.349 --> 00:06:31.680
western knock-off of the traditional Japanese
samurai weapon.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:36.600
The metal it was forged from seemed to be
unpolished, unsharpened, and unbalanced.

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:42.590
Overall, it just seemed a bit of a mess, even
to those in the office unfamiliar with katanas

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:45.430
or their cultural significance in Japan.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:50.949
Yet, when he described it, Martin seemed enamored
with the sword, citing how incredible the

00:06:50.949 --> 00:06:55.830
balance was and how the obviously very blunt
weapon could more easily slice through solid

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:59.110
steel than one of those infomercial knives.

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:02.969
Of course, the more pressing and unsettling
question for most of the employees was why

00:07:02.969 --> 00:07:07.360
the hell did their boss think it was okay
to bring a katana into the office?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.319
When any of the staff working there built
up enough courage to approach their ‘eccentric’

00:07:11.319 --> 00:07:16.119
sword-toting boss to ask him, Martin would
simply state that it was a measure to encourage

00:07:16.119 --> 00:07:17.909
more productivity.

00:07:17.909 --> 00:07:21.729
If he was unhappy with the coding work his
programmers were doing, or the content being

00:07:21.729 --> 00:07:26.960
posted to his social media site, Martin would
start strutting around the office.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:32.840
His head was always tilted back, smugly looking
down his nose at his staff – who he’d

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:36.619
sometimes affectionately call his ‘underlings’
or ‘drones’.

00:07:36.619 --> 00:07:40.849
With a look of self-important superiority
and one hand constantly resting on the hilt

00:07:40.849 --> 00:07:47.110
of his katana, his ‘productivity patrols’
managed to put everyone in the office on edge.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:52.159
Less because they were threatened by the blunted
sword or Martin’s unimposing five-and-a-half-foot

00:07:52.159 --> 00:07:57.569
stature, but more because the staff all agreed
that what he was doing was just plain weird.

00:07:57.569 --> 00:08:01.259
One morning, Ned, one of the staff members
working at the office, was casually sitting

00:08:01.259 --> 00:08:06.870
at his computer, working his way through rewriting
a few lines of code as he’d been asked to.

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:10.909
Suddenly, he felt something cold and metal
resting on his right shoulder and felt the

00:08:10.909 --> 00:08:15.659
presence of someone leaning over him uncomfortably
close on the left.

00:08:15.659 --> 00:08:20.009
Immediately his heart jumped in surprise and
fear, only to instantly drop back down to

00:08:20.009 --> 00:08:24.409
a normal beat when he remembered that Martin’s
sword was barely sharper than a butter knife.

00:08:24.409 --> 00:08:27.259
“Hey, Mr. Zeepleburger,” Ned sighed.

00:08:27.259 --> 00:08:30.309
“Hey there, Nedry,” Martin replied.

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:34.340
His voice sounded like he was trying to smile,
but also didn’t know how long it was normal

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:35.340
to hold it.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:37.710
Also, Ned’s name wasn’t short for Nedry.

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:43.099
“You know, you were asked to finish up this
coding an hour ago,” he continued, even

00:08:43.099 --> 00:08:46.800
though Ned had only been told the code needed
rewriting that long ago.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:52.340
“If you don’t hurry up, I might just have
to chop you into bits with my huge sword.”

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:56.430
Martin forced a laugh, as though he’d never
actually expressed humor before.

00:08:56.430 --> 00:09:00.540
Eventually, the employees had grown sick of
Martin brandishing his katana around the office.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:04.880
They didn’t feel threatened, so much as
they were just annoyed; it was distracting

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:07.060
them from actually doing their jobs.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:12.200
When a group of them, led by Ned, marched
into his office to formally complain in solidarity,

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:17.070
Martin spun around to face them in his desk
chair, his useless sword in his hand.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:21.640
“So, this is treason then,” he smiled
to himself as if he’d been waiting for this

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:23.720
moment, drawing the katana.

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:27.990
In his head, Martin was about to leap forward
over his desk, in a move ripped straight out

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:29.500
of a Star Wars movie.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:33.340
He thought he would easily spin through the
air, hurtling towards his group of employees

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:37.970
with the blade ready to skewer the nearest
ones for daring to question his leadership.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:42.730
Unfortunately, despite his surfing trips in
Hawaii, Martin wasn’t exactly nimble enough

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:43.840
to pull it off.

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:48.140
He barely jumped high enough off the ground
to clear the desk, knocking the whole thing

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:50.010
forward and tumbling over it.

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:53.740
Landing awkwardly, the tip of the blade barely
reached far enough to lightly graze Ned at

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:54.890
the front of the group.

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:58.890
Instead, all of Martin’s employees looked
at him pathetically laying face-down on the

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:00.340
office carpet.

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:04.870
After changing hands who knows exactly how
many times, the Katana of Apparent Invincibility

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:10.030
would soon find itself in the hands of another
soul just as worthy of wielding it… and

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:13.090
making themselves look really dumb in the
process.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:17.530
For as long as he could remember, Zac had
been obsessed with superheroes.

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:22.470
He had spent his youth reading comic books,
idolizing characters like Batman who fought

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:26.880
criminals on the mean streets to deliver swift
and brutal justice.

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:32.410
Even as he got older, Zac never outgrew that
childhood dream he had held onto: to become

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:34.040
a real-life superhero.

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:38.930
Now, obviously, he knew that superhuman powers
were a little out of his reach.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:43.940
But that never stopped Bruce Wayne; Zac could
train himself, build up his physical strength

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:45.530
and learn to fight.

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:49.180
Of course, he overlooked the part where Bruce
Wayne also had billions of dollars inherited

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:54.340
from his parents at his disposal, not to mention
a cave with lots of fancy high-tech gadgets,

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:58.500
an English butler, and had trained under some
of the most skilled hand to hand combatants

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:00.360
in the entire world.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:04.990
Batman never learned karate during night classes
held at the local community college.

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:09.410
Still, there was nothing that could deter
Zac from his heroic aspirations.

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:13.740
He spent every free moment he had in the gym,
lifting weights, and building his biceps to

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:15.850
the size of burger buns.

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:20.540
After failing his exam twice, he achieved
the coveted blue belt in his martial arts

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:25.130
class, and he even ordered the parts he would
need to construct his super suit.

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:30.170
Sure, Zac told himself, it might have just
looked like a ski mask and some hockey pads,

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:33.050
but he needed freedom of movement as well
as protection.

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:38.220
There was only one piece left to complete
this stage of his origin story: a kickass

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:40.120
superhero codename.

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:46.220
That was when fate seemed to step in, taking
its rarest of forms: an eBay listing for a

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:47.870
used sword.

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:51.360
From the moment he saw it, Zac knew he needed
to own it.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:55.510
Not all superheroes used weapons, but he figured
it would be a good deterrent.

00:11:55.510 --> 00:12:00.930
He’d only ever draw his blade to wound,
and only when there was no other option.

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:05.430
As he placed his bid, Captain Katana was born.

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:10.570
It was his first nightly patrol; Zac had donned
his protective suit and concealed his secret

00:12:10.570 --> 00:12:12.130
identity behind the mask.

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:17.160
The katana was sheathed and strapped to his
back, for now, but he was sure enough it would

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:21.110
soon see its share of righteous vengeance
before the night was over.

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:25.131
Well, more accurately, it would cause more
than its share of mishaps by the end of the

00:12:25.131 --> 00:12:26.131
night.

00:12:26.131 --> 00:12:30.820
But Zac… sorry, ‘Captain Katana’ didn’t
care.

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:35.730
He felt unstoppable, in fact, ever since the
sword had arrived in the mail, he had been

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.300
feeling like he could take on the world.

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:42.400
The would-be hero thought it was just the
anticipation of finally being what he’d

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:46.980
always wanted to be, exactly what his training
had been preparing for.

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:51.570
How was he to know that the sword itself was
the reason for his dangerous amount of overconfidence?

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:56.620
You see, while it might not be imbued with
ancient magic, the power of a god, or the

00:12:56.620 --> 00:13:01.940
ability to suck the souls of its victims,
there is one thing remarkable about SCP-572.

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:08.440
Okay, well, two things; the first being just
how bad it is as a sword.

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:13.490
It isn’t forged from any high-quality steel,
or made by an elusive Japanese swordsmith.

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:18.100
Whereas a katana made with the proper amount
of skill, craftsmanship, and care is perfectly

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:23.670
weighted, and balanced evenly for the right
amount of speed and swiftness in combat, this

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:26.610
one is… well, none of the above.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:31.540
And as if it wasn’t bad enough that it lacked
all the other qualities of a true katana,

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:34.230
SCP-572’s blade is totally blunt.

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:36.860
Seriously, you couldn’t even slice bread
with this thing.

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:42.150
And yet, in his heart, Zac felt like it was
the perfect weapon, the most powerful tool

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:44.580
in his vigilante war on crime.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:49.100
Speaking of crimes, he thought he’d found
his first prey for his nightly hunt.

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:54.040
The sound of a car alarm was blaring through
the city streets, coming from somewhere nearby.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:59.730
Our woefully underequipped and underprepared
hero raced a few blocks over to find the source.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:04.310
From a distance, all he could see was a man
fumbling with the door of a locked car, clearly

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:07.760
unable to open it and trying to force his
way in.

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:12.029
What this so-called hero didn’t think to
do was assess the situation for any further

00:14:12.029 --> 00:14:15.130
context, too quick to trust in his ‘instincts’.

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:21.060
“Stop right there, thief!” he declared,
unable to hear how muffled his voice sounded

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:24.290
when filtered through the material of the
ski mask.

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:28.840
The man froze and turned to look at the figure
approaching him, only to raise an eyebrow

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.060
in confusion.

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:32.390
“Um… hello?” he called back.

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:33.920
“Can I help you?”

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:38.670
“Silence villain,” the masked onlooker
shouted, just audible over the noisy car alarm.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:43.500
“You’ve got two choices here: either you
walk away, leave that person’s property

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.620
alone and I’ll let you off with a warning.

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:48.939
Or, we do this the hard way, and you’ll
face…”

00:14:48.939 --> 00:14:52.700
Zac paused for dramatic effect, like he had
practiced in the mirror.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:55.040
“The wrath of Captain Katana!”

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:56.680
“Of who?”

00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:57.680
the other man replied.

00:14:57.680 --> 00:15:02.290
“Look man, I’m not sure what your deal
is, if this some kind of cosplay thing or

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:03.330
you’re just… nuts.

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:05.800
But this is my car, okay?

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:09.350
The door gets stuck, I just need to jimmy
it a little sometimes, but it sets the alarm

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:10.350
off.”

00:15:10.350 --> 00:15:11.350
“Liar!”

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:13.400
Captain Katana yelled, reaching over his shoulder.

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:17.029
His gloved hand gripped the hilt of his weapon
and pulled it free of its sheath.

00:15:17.029 --> 00:15:21.070
From across the parking lot, the driver couldn’t
tell how utterly useless the sword was at

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:22.529
his current distance.

00:15:22.529 --> 00:15:27.700
All he saw was a masked, potentially unhinged,
stranger dramatically pacing towards him with

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.950
what was very clearly a weapon.

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:34.290
“What the hell?” he exclaimed, urgently
trying to get his car door open.

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:38.770
The handle gave way and the door sprung open,
allowing the man to hurriedly climb into the

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:41.420
diver’s seat and shut the door behind him.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:44.950
Starting the engine, the lights came on and
illuminated the stranger in front of him,

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:49.410
who stood looking absolutely ridiculous in
his outfit; consisting of what looked like

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:51.000
various pieces of sportswear.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:56.130
Katana in hand, the ‘superhero’ was still
striding slowly towards the car as the engine

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:57.860
spluttered into life.

00:15:57.860 --> 00:16:02.320
Zac stopped, smiling under the material of
his hockey mask, as he gripped both hands

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:04.710
around the hilt and took a wide stance.

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:09.580
Flooring the accelerator, the driver was eager
to get away from this obvious lunatic, even

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:13.779
if he was wielding a sword that was mostly
unusable; it didn’t seem like that would

00:16:13.779 --> 00:16:19.750
stop Captain Katana from trying to use it,
no matter how unsuccessfully.

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:24.180
The car came barrelling towards Zac, and he
readied himself, lifting the blade high above

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:25.180
his head.

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:29.200
He knew that he would be able to bring it
downwards in a vicious swipe at precisely

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:30.440
the right moment.

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:35.300
The second the worn-out, dull metal connected
with that of the car, it would slice the ‘stolen’

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:42.029
vehicle into two perfect pieces, split right
down the middle, leaving the ‘thief’ confounded

00:16:42.029 --> 00:16:44.490
and ready to be handed over to the police.

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:47.480
You can already guess that’s not what happened,
can’t you?

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:51.730
With barely a screech of tires against the
concrete and without even enough distance

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:55.890
to build up much speed, the car headed straight
for Captain Katana.

00:16:55.890 --> 00:17:00.980
He made a flailing, uncoordinated swing far
too early, causing the sword to bounce right

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:02.550
off the hood of the car.

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:06.799
The force of the impact wasn’t huge, but
it was enough to cause the katana to slip

00:17:06.799 --> 00:17:10.999
from the wannabe hero’s hands; helped by
the fact his gloves didn’t have that much

00:17:10.999 --> 00:17:12.049
grip on them.

00:17:12.049 --> 00:17:16.600
The Katana of Apparent Invincibility was sent
sailing through the air, and came clattering

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:20.030
to the ground, rolling under another car in
the parking lot.

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:23.819
Although, Zac was a little preoccupied to
see where it landed.

00:17:23.819 --> 00:17:28.110
No sooner had he lost his grip on his ‘almighty
weapon of justice’, around three and a half

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:31.340
thousand pounds of metal collided with Captain
Katana.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:35.210
Felled on his first ever night as a superhero
by his very first villain.

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:40.730
Still, Zac at least learned what his Kryptonite
was, his greatest weakness, just like so many

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:42.779
classic superheroes had.

00:17:42.779 --> 00:17:46.380
His just happened to be being hit by a mid-size
sedan.

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:49.909
Tumbling back onto the ground, the back of
Captain Katana’s head thumped heavily against

00:17:49.909 --> 00:17:55.159
cold, hard concrete, leaving him with a concussion
and an overwhelming sense of embarrassment

00:17:55.159 --> 00:17:57.830
as the driver parked his car and called an
ambulance.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:01.409
At least he now knew he never wanted to pick
up that sword again.

00:18:01.409 --> 00:18:06.789
You see, that’s the second remarkable thing
about SCP-572.

00:18:06.789 --> 00:18:10.490
Anyone who picks it up instantly perceives
it as a mighty weapon, the kind you would

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:12.720
find in an ancient legend.

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:17.080
Despite the sword being crudely made, blunt,
and generally unfit for any use, the wielder

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:21.690
will maintain the belief that it not only
has perfect balance and cutting power, but

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:27.580
that the sword has also imbued them with unparalleled
strength and invincibility to damage.

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:31.860
It's all a delusion, of course, and whoever
holds that sword will gladly prove it to you.

00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:36.070
They’ll try to perform incredibly risky
stunts with it, only to end up severely injuring

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:37.419
themselves in the process.

00:18:37.419 --> 00:18:43.399
Don’t worry though, if you ever come across
SCP-572, it’s nothing a quick thump in the

00:18:43.399 --> 00:18:44.840
back of the head won’t fix.

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:50.409
Now, if you want to hear about an actual all-powerful
sword that can obliterate anything on an atomic

00:18:50.409 --> 00:18:54.990
level, as well as the ancient energy building
who wields it, then you should go and check

00:18:54.990 --> 00:18:57.610
out “SCP-001 THE GATE GUARDIAN”.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:03.090
And, of course, sometimes the only thing better
than one katana is two katanas and an infamous

00:19:03.090 --> 00:19:04.249
comic book character.

00:19:04.249 --> 00:19:07.820
But will that be enough to take on the Hard
to Destroy Reptile?

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:10.619
Find out in “DEADPOOL vs SCP-682”!

